        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Due to an illness during the return journey of his European tour, David Garrick remained in Paris from late August or early September 1764 until his departure and return to London in April 1765. He likely ordered his tea service during that time, probably from a <i>marchand-mercier</i>."@en .

